WEBVTT

00:00:02.980 --> 00:00:05.980
Things are getting busier and busier.

00:00:05.980 --> 00:00:08.230
The culture festival's almost here.

00:00:07.110 --> 00:00:08.230
days until Shimotsuki Festival!!

00:00:08.570 --> 00:00:11.360
I wonder what we should do for it...

00:00:17.700 --> 00:00:20.870
What does the cosplay research club even do?

00:00:20.870 --> 00:00:24.920
We only created the club as a front
for gathering the fragments...

00:00:24.920 --> 00:00:28.040
Well, since we have the chance,
we might as well do something, right?

00:00:28.340 --> 00:00:29.670
Yeah, I'd like to do something.

00:00:29.670 --> 00:00:30.920
I am unopposed.

00:00:31.420 --> 00:00:33.840
We could do a costume parade or a fashion show.

00:00:33.840 --> 00:00:34.630
That's wonderful!

00:00:34.630 --> 00:00:37.970
H-Hold on! You mean with the five of us?

00:00:37.970 --> 00:00:39.930
Yes. You like that stuff, don't you?

00:00:40.850 --> 00:00:42.810
I... I don't really...

00:00:43.270 --> 00:00:46.690
If we start making costumes now,
will we finish in time?

00:00:46.690 --> 00:00:47.690
For starters,

00:00:47.690 --> 00:00:51.940
we could use the ones from the
theater festival, plus a few new ones.

00:00:52.820 --> 00:00:55.820
Yeah, something frilly and cute would be nice.

00:00:56.820 --> 00:00:58.200
What's wrong, Subaru?

00:00:59.450 --> 00:01:00.330
I...

00:01:00.790 --> 00:01:02.950
I'm in the astronomy club!

00:01:16.680 --> 00:01:18.550
After-School Pleiades

00:01:19.220 --> 00:01:24.730
Sobbingly, I went on my journey

00:01:24.770 --> 00:01:29.190
Wishing I could at least fly through the sky

00:01:30.320 --> 00:01:35.570
And yet the stars gently shone on me in the nights after our quarrels

00:01:35.570 --> 00:01:41.120
I wonder if you were also watching them

00:01:41.120 --> 00:01:46.370
I don't know... I want to know... I want to feel it...

00:01:46.370 --> 00:01:53.420
Nothingness simply means there are infinite possibilities

00:01:54.760 --> 00:01:57.220
The excitement I got after realizing that

00:01:57.220 --> 00:02:00.300
was like surfing the waves of space and time

00:02:00.140 --> 00:02:05.390
How strange that I'm not afraid anymore

00:02:05.390 --> 00:02:08.100
Let's embrace our imperfections and go on

00:02:08.100 --> 00:02:10.980
We'll open the promised door

00:02:10.980 --> 00:02:16.150
and gain dazzling smiles!

00:02:33.000 --> 00:02:38.010
Planetarium Rendezvous

00:02:38.880 --> 00:02:41.800
I'm glad we managed to borrow
the observatory room.

00:02:41.800 --> 00:02:42.720
Yeah!

00:02:42.720 --> 00:02:45.970
It's thanks to your help
with the project proposal.

00:02:49.520 --> 00:02:52.060
So you decided to just put
the costumes on display?

00:02:52.060 --> 00:02:55.570
Yeah. Aoi was too embarrassed to go further.

00:02:57.280 --> 00:03:00.950
We also plan to open up the club room
so others can try cosplaying.

00:03:00.950 --> 00:03:01.950
Sounds fun.

00:03:01.950 --> 00:03:05.410
We all know you actually
wanted to do it, Aoi-chin.

00:03:05.410 --> 00:03:07.500
We shouldn't stand out too much, right?

00:03:07.500 --> 00:03:09.290
Our club started as—

00:03:08.830 --> 00:03:09.290
Yes!

00:03:09.750 --> 00:03:11.210
Aoi is right!

00:03:11.500 --> 00:03:12.380
What do you mean?

00:03:12.670 --> 00:03:15.500
The barrier around this room is
known as a "double-connector type."

00:03:15.500 --> 00:03:17.300
It works with the power
compressing the fragments

00:03:17.300 --> 00:03:21.010
to form a powerful security device by
continuously expanding their power.

00:03:21.010 --> 00:03:22.300
Lowering the barrier for

00:03:22.300 --> 00:03:25.350
the culture festival to let countless
students, siblings, and parents

00:03:25.350 --> 00:03:27.220
into the room is far too insecure!

00:03:27.220 --> 00:03:28.270
You're right.

00:03:28.680 --> 00:03:31.390
We worked together to gather
the engine fragments.

00:03:31.390 --> 00:03:32.770
We should be careful with them.

00:03:33.230 --> 00:03:36.150
There's no guarantee he won't
show up again, either.

00:03:36.150 --> 00:03:39.990
Yes, we all must protect these
fragments, no matter what!

00:03:40.490 --> 00:03:44.490
But if we do nothing, they'll say
our club isn't doing any activities,

00:03:44.490 --> 00:03:46.490
and we'll lose the right to use this room.

00:03:46.780 --> 00:03:47.160
Huh?

00:03:47.160 --> 00:03:48.700
If we lose the club room,

00:03:48.700 --> 00:03:53.040
we'll lose our place to hide the fragments,
we'll lose our base, and...

00:03:53.040 --> 00:03:57.550
Your position as president of our
group will be threatened, as well.

00:03:58.750 --> 00:04:01.170
Um, should I hold on to them?

00:04:02.510 --> 00:04:06.760
The times people are allowed to enter the
astronomy club's planetarium are limited.

00:04:06.760 --> 00:04:09.520
And at all other times, it's locked.

00:04:09.520 --> 00:04:11.520
I guess that's better than leaving them here.

00:04:11.930 --> 00:04:14.270
I doubt that many people will come, anyway.

00:04:15.270 --> 00:04:17.320
Subaru! Sniffle...

00:04:21.190 --> 00:04:23.740
Subaru, is that for the planetarium?

00:04:23.740 --> 00:04:25.200
Oh, yeah.

00:04:25.200 --> 00:04:27.450
You punch small holes in it like this,

00:04:27.450 --> 00:04:31.160
and when you shine light from
inside, it projects outward.

00:04:31.160 --> 00:04:33.540
Wow, is this all of them?

00:04:33.920 --> 00:04:35.790
No, just the major ones.

00:04:35.790 --> 00:04:38.710
How do you shine light from the inside?

00:04:38.710 --> 00:04:42.380
Well, when you put each
of these sheets together,

00:04:42.380 --> 00:04:45.380
it forms a dome called a "fixed-star sphere"...

00:04:45.380 --> 00:04:46.260
Subaru...

00:04:47.140 --> 00:04:49.930
Here's the bedside lamp you requested.

00:04:50.310 --> 00:04:51.220
Lamp?

00:04:51.220 --> 00:04:53.230
Wow, thanks, Nanako!

00:04:53.230 --> 00:04:54.140
I get it!

00:04:54.390 --> 00:04:57.270
You place that fixed-star sphere over this light!

00:04:57.270 --> 00:04:59.150
It's not just that.

00:04:59.770 --> 00:05:03.400
There are five different settings
for the rotation speed.

00:05:04.360 --> 00:05:06.410
I hope it works.

00:05:08.030 --> 00:05:10.370
Oh, I need to head off.

00:05:10.370 --> 00:05:12.540
Will you be all right on your own?

00:05:12.540 --> 00:05:13.290
Yeah.

00:05:13.290 --> 00:05:16.500
I have someone helping me, so I'll be fine.

00:05:16.500 --> 00:05:17.250
Later!

00:05:22.460 --> 00:05:26.340
L-Looks like her planetarium is going smoothly.

00:05:26.340 --> 00:05:27.760
You mean her boyfriend, right?

00:05:27.760 --> 00:05:28.510
Bo—

00:05:29.220 --> 00:05:30.140
Boyfriend?

00:05:30.140 --> 00:05:31.510
Want to go spy on them?

00:05:31.510 --> 00:05:32.720
We can't do that!

00:05:32.720 --> 00:05:34.600
Why not?

00:05:34.930 --> 00:05:38.020
At times like these, friends are
supposed to watch from a distance.

00:05:38.020 --> 00:05:41.110
You don't care if he makes your precious
Subaru cry without your knowing?

00:05:41.110 --> 00:05:43.230
She's with an upperclassman
we know nothing about.

00:05:43.230 --> 00:05:46.400
That's right. We need to research
him, and watch over them!

00:05:46.400 --> 00:05:50.160
Y-Yeah... You're right.

00:05:50.200 --> 00:05:50.280
Shimotsuki

00:05:50.200 --> 00:05:50.280
Festival

00:05:50.280 --> 00:05:50.370
Shimotsuki

00:05:50.280 --> 00:05:50.370
Festival

00:05:50.280 --> 00:05:50.370
Best Couple Contest

00:05:52.120 --> 00:05:52.160
~For Blushing Young Couples~

00:05:52.120 --> 00:05:52.160
Seeking Contestants

00:05:52.120 --> 00:05:52.160
Participation condition: Must be in a lovely relationship. Nominations may be made by yourself or others.

00:05:59.000 --> 00:06:00.840
This is it!

00:06:09.800 --> 00:06:10.640
Hey.

00:06:10.640 --> 00:06:12.760
Ah, sorry to keep you waiting.

00:06:13.100 --> 00:06:15.100
Yeah, I waited for you.

00:06:18.270 --> 00:06:22.900
So everyone's making the costumes
to put on display right now.

00:06:22.900 --> 00:06:23.770
I see.

00:06:23.770 --> 00:06:28.650
Aoi's complaining,
but I think she actually enjoys it.

00:06:33.660 --> 00:06:34.290
Hold on.

00:06:34.290 --> 00:06:35.080
Huh?

00:06:37.040 --> 00:06:39.250
You look kind of unsteady.

00:06:39.710 --> 00:06:41.790
Th-Thanks...

00:06:43.960 --> 00:06:46.670
<i>Can you find the three stars
lined up next to each other</i>

00:06:46.670 --> 00:06:49.010
<i>like friends in the winter night sky?</i>

00:06:49.680 --> 00:06:50.840
<i>With those three at its center,</i>

00:06:50.840 --> 00:06:54.010
<i>the first-magnitude star above
and to the left is Betelgeuse,</i>

00:06:54.010 --> 00:06:55.680
<i>the one below and to the right is Rigel</i>

00:06:55.680 --> 00:07:01.850
<i>and together, the hourglass-shaped constellation they form is known as Orion.</i>

00:07:02.560 --> 00:07:06.900
<i>If you look directly left from Orion's Betelgeuse,</i>

00:07:06.900 --> 00:07:09.570
<i>you find Canis Minor's
first-magnitude star, Procyon.</i>

00:07:09.570 --> 00:07:14.240
<i>Below Betelgeuse and Procyon,
joining them into an equilateral triangle,</i>

00:07:14.240 --> 00:07:16.950
<i>is another first-magnitude star, Sirius.</i>

00:07:16.950 --> 00:07:21.120
<i>Together, this trio of first-magnitude stars
forms what we call the "winter triangle."</i>

00:07:21.750 --> 00:07:23.210
H-How is it?

00:07:23.210 --> 00:07:23.880
Yes.

00:07:24.500 --> 00:07:29.420
Your examples for picturing the shapes of
the constellations were very easy to follow.

00:07:29.420 --> 00:07:31.800
Really? That's good.

00:07:31.800 --> 00:07:32.970
Subaru!

00:07:32.970 --> 00:07:34.350
Use this now.

00:07:36.970 --> 00:07:38.640
Something's glowing...

00:07:38.640 --> 00:07:40.020
It's the fragments.

00:07:40.270 --> 00:07:41.350
The fragments?

00:07:41.640 --> 00:07:46.520
I thought handing the fragments over in their
natural form would still be dangerous.

00:07:46.520 --> 00:07:48.070
So I changed them into a different shape,

00:07:48.070 --> 00:07:50.780
and placed the same kind of barrier
on them as around this room.

00:07:50.780 --> 00:07:52.410
That's surprisingly clever.

00:07:52.780 --> 00:07:54.120
I'm counting on you, Subaru!

00:07:54.120 --> 00:07:55.450
Yes!

00:07:55.830 --> 00:07:56.950
By the way, Subarun!

00:07:56.950 --> 00:07:59.540
Shouldn't you be heading to
the astronomy club by now?

00:07:59.540 --> 00:08:02.040
Huh? But there's still another hour...

00:08:02.040 --> 00:08:03.000
Subarun!

00:08:03.250 --> 00:08:03.750
Yes!

00:08:04.100 --> 00:08:06.250
Aside from you, are there any
astronomy club members?

00:08:06.590 --> 00:08:08.210
Just me...

00:08:08.210 --> 00:08:12.760
Then leave this place to us,
and head to the astronomy club!

00:08:13.130 --> 00:08:14.470
H-Huh?

00:08:15.590 --> 00:08:16.550
R-Really?

00:08:16.550 --> 00:08:17.600
Yes, yes, yes!

00:08:18.010 --> 00:08:21.310
Thank you... I'll do that, then.

00:08:30.110 --> 00:08:32.400
Wow, this is great.

00:08:32.820 --> 00:08:35.070
Have you been taking hidden photos?

00:08:35.320 --> 00:08:36.320
This, too?

00:08:36.570 --> 00:08:37.580
And this one?

00:08:38.080 --> 00:08:39.950
Did you take these, Nanako?

00:08:41.080 --> 00:08:44.460
If we'd tried to take them openly,
they would've been embarrassed.

00:08:45.370 --> 00:08:50.250
To enter them, we need a photo of them
together and an interview with them.

00:08:50.250 --> 00:08:51.710
How they started dating,

00:08:51.710 --> 00:08:54.880
what they like about each other, what they
wish were different about each other...

00:08:54.880 --> 00:08:56.090
Now that we have these photos,

00:08:56.090 --> 00:08:59.310
we just need to catch them together
and spring an interview on them.

00:08:59.310 --> 00:09:00.390
Catch them?

00:09:10.610 --> 00:09:13.070
Th-The winter constellations are done!

00:09:13.530 --> 00:09:15.610
Could we test them real quick?

00:09:15.610 --> 00:09:18.370
Yeah, let's do that.

00:09:22.330 --> 00:09:24.210
Um, thank you.

00:09:25.120 --> 00:09:26.080
For what?

00:09:26.580 --> 00:09:30.340
For helping me out with the astronomy club,
when you aren't even a member.

00:09:30.840 --> 00:09:34.970
You helped with my gardening, didn't you?

00:09:37.890 --> 00:09:40.970
That was because those were precious flowers.

00:09:42.310 --> 00:09:47.020
Those flowers brought us back together.

00:09:49.730 --> 00:09:50.980
Those flowers...

00:09:51.820 --> 00:09:54.530
It was a very pretty greenhouse, but...

00:09:55.490 --> 00:10:01.580
I felt like, maybe, you always
wanted to leave it, Minato.

00:10:03.410 --> 00:10:04.370
You...

00:10:06.080 --> 00:10:09.670
You may have been the one who
opened the door for me.

00:10:10.880 --> 00:10:14.420
But that wasn't what I wished for.

00:10:22.810 --> 00:10:24.930
Now, let's test it.

00:10:25.770 --> 00:10:26.680
Yeah.

00:10:35.030 --> 00:10:39.820
We need to re-tape that spot.
Some light is escaping.

00:10:40.910 --> 00:10:43.830
We'll have to slow the rotation, too.

00:10:46.450 --> 00:10:49.960
I guess it just isn't the same as actual outer space.

00:11:01.590 --> 00:11:03.680
Do you want to see actual outer space?

00:11:04.970 --> 00:11:06.310
Um...

00:11:08.520 --> 00:11:11.600
I'm sure everyone would like to see that.

00:11:14.980 --> 00:11:16.940
Then let's go there now.

00:11:17.280 --> 00:11:18.070
Huh?

00:11:28.200 --> 00:11:30.660
H-Huh? This is...

00:11:32.830 --> 00:11:34.500
Wow...

00:11:46.010 --> 00:11:48.520
day until Shimotsuki Festival!!

00:11:50.180 --> 00:11:51.890
Wow...

00:11:52.600 --> 00:11:55.270
It's like a real planetarium.

00:11:57.190 --> 00:11:59.570
This is outer space. The real thing.

00:12:00.030 --> 00:12:02.780
But none of the constellations I know are here.

00:12:02.780 --> 00:12:06.990
Of course not. This is outside
of our solar system.

00:12:07.790 --> 00:12:09.580
Am I dreaming?

00:12:10.120 --> 00:12:11.620
Look, over there.

00:12:12.500 --> 00:12:14.380
That's our Sun.

00:12:15.040 --> 00:12:18.550
Right this moment, your friends are down there,

00:12:18.550 --> 00:12:20.920
preparing for the culture festival.

00:12:22.300 --> 00:12:23.800
But that's...

00:12:23.800 --> 00:12:25.510
Yes, impossible.

00:12:26.140 --> 00:12:29.930
Your body isn't capable of
exceeding the speed of light,

00:12:30.350 --> 00:12:33.140
and in the vacuum of space,
you shouldn't be able to act.

00:12:33.980 --> 00:12:38.770
At the moment, we're also outside
of this universe's laws.

00:12:39.400 --> 00:12:41.650
I-I don't get it.

00:12:42.280 --> 00:12:44.700
By etching our data onto this space,

00:12:45.070 --> 00:12:49.740
we're making this universe believe that
our bodies are here right now.

00:12:50.080 --> 00:12:54.330
Though we do currently exist in this space,
we also don't exist in any space.

00:12:54.330 --> 00:12:58.000
Is this a scientific thing or...

00:12:58.250 --> 00:13:01.380
Who knows? Perhaps it's magic.

00:13:01.760 --> 00:13:03.130
Magic...

00:13:03.510 --> 00:13:05.380
Let's just enjoy the moment, Subaru.

00:13:10.060 --> 00:13:13.020
Incredible! The stars are flowing by!

00:13:16.440 --> 00:13:18.190
Projecting! Do Not Enter

00:13:17.690 --> 00:13:19.270
Th-This is...

00:13:19.270 --> 00:13:21.980
It looks like the planetarium is
in the middle of testing.

00:13:21.980 --> 00:13:23.440
Huh? Then...

00:13:23.440 --> 00:13:26.570
They're alone, together, in a dark room.

00:13:26.910 --> 00:13:28.070
Okay, let's open the door!

00:13:28.070 --> 00:13:30.330
Don't! Hikaru, Aoi!

00:13:30.330 --> 00:13:33.200
B-But we need to get that interview with them...

00:13:33.200 --> 00:13:36.460
If we go in now, we really will be interfering!

00:13:39.790 --> 00:13:41.210
All right.

00:13:47.550 --> 00:13:48.970
On second thought, I can't leave!

00:13:50.510 --> 00:13:54.430
If I don't check on them right now,
I won't be able to sleep tonight!

00:13:54.430 --> 00:13:54.480
Projecting! Do Not Enter

00:13:54.680 --> 00:13:57.690
Wait, Itsuki! We should open it together!

00:14:01.230 --> 00:14:03.400
Huh? Where are they?

00:14:04.280 --> 00:14:05.900
Wow, it's so bright!

00:14:06.860 --> 00:14:08.160
Can you tell where we are?

00:14:09.740 --> 00:14:12.080
There are lots of blue stars...

00:14:13.160 --> 00:14:15.450
Is this the Pleiades star cluster?

00:14:15.450 --> 00:14:17.830
Yes. Its Japanese name is "Subaru."

00:14:17.830 --> 00:14:19.790
The same as your name.

00:14:20.250 --> 00:14:23.670
One of the other meanings
of "Subaru" is "to unite."

00:14:24.170 --> 00:14:28.550
The Pleiades star cluster is composed
of over one hundred fixed stars.

00:14:28.880 --> 00:14:32.930
It's very pretty, but I can't keep my eyes open.

00:14:37.520 --> 00:14:38.940
This is...

00:14:39.980 --> 00:14:40.900
Wow...

00:14:41.270 --> 00:14:43.520
Now we're a bit farther away.

00:14:43.520 --> 00:14:46.650
We're on some planet, in some other galaxy.

00:14:47.110 --> 00:14:52.160
This galaxy is about to
collide with another galaxy.

00:14:52.620 --> 00:14:58.160
If we could see this view from Earth...
It would be the Andromeda Galaxy?

00:14:58.160 --> 00:15:04.420
Yes. In two or three billion years,
this view will be visible from Earth.

00:15:04.880 --> 00:15:07.550
We'll have to think up new constellations.

00:15:20.770 --> 00:15:23.230
Now we're back in our galaxy.

00:15:23.230 --> 00:15:26.570
This is the center, its liveliest spot.

00:15:27.860 --> 00:15:31.110
There are so many stars,
space doesn't look dark.

00:15:31.820 --> 00:15:34.780
How far does space reach?

00:15:35.160 --> 00:15:37.240
How long does it go on?

00:15:38.000 --> 00:15:39.000
Subaru?

00:15:40.710 --> 00:15:43.670
It's a bit scary to think there's no end to it.

00:15:45.840 --> 00:15:46.670
Sorry.

00:15:46.920 --> 00:15:50.630
Huh? No, I don't mean that... I'm having fun!

00:15:51.800 --> 00:15:55.680
I was cold to you earlier.

00:15:56.100 --> 00:15:59.140
Maybe I'm the one who's afraid.

00:15:59.600 --> 00:16:03.310
Is that why you invited me into space?

00:16:03.850 --> 00:16:05.190
It is.

00:16:07.110 --> 00:16:11.030
Then you should have fun, too.

00:16:11.950 --> 00:16:12.860
Yeah.

00:16:13.570 --> 00:16:14.620
For now.

00:16:16.030 --> 00:16:20.500
Right now, we're traveling
outside this universe's laws.

00:16:21.370 --> 00:16:25.040
So we won't be able to bring our
memories of this trip home with us.

00:16:25.330 --> 00:16:26.460
We'll forget it?

00:16:27.340 --> 00:16:29.590
We can't go home without forgetting it,

00:16:29.590 --> 00:16:33.470
but because we'll forget it,
we can enjoy these sights now.

00:16:34.430 --> 00:16:36.090
I see.

00:16:38.060 --> 00:16:41.350
Do you think it's pointless to
see anything if we'll forget it?

00:16:43.390 --> 00:16:46.360
I think I recognize this feeling.

00:16:47.810 --> 00:16:49.650
I used to do this all the time.

00:16:50.690 --> 00:16:56.870
When I was little, my mother was
hospitalized for a short while.

00:16:57.780 --> 00:17:00.540
I went to visit her every day with my father.

00:17:00.540 --> 00:17:03.790
Gynecology

00:17:00.540 --> 00:17:03.790
Obstetrics

00:17:00.540 --> 00:17:03.790
Pediatrics

00:17:01.790 --> 00:17:05.170
But one day, I got lost.

00:17:18.180 --> 00:17:20.890
It was a very mysterious room.

00:17:20.890 --> 00:17:25.440
Light was shining from the floor, walls, and ceiling.

00:17:28.860 --> 00:17:30.230
Who are you?

00:17:31.780 --> 00:17:34.070
You can see better from over here.

00:17:34.900 --> 00:17:36.320
Sit there.

00:17:46.420 --> 00:17:47.040
Huh?

00:17:49.790 --> 00:17:51.040
Don't be afraid.

00:17:52.550 --> 00:17:53.510
It's all right.

00:17:54.010 --> 00:17:56.130
I can use magic.

00:17:59.470 --> 00:18:00.640
From then on,

00:18:00.890 --> 00:18:02.760
every time I visited my mother,

00:18:02.760 --> 00:18:04.890
I also visited that boy's room.

00:18:05.180 --> 00:18:07.020
We would look at the stars together,

00:18:07.020 --> 00:18:09.270
and talk about them a lot.

00:18:11.570 --> 00:18:14.280
That's Betelgeuse, a red supergiant.

00:18:14.570 --> 00:18:17.700
It's an old star that's expanded
and grown red with age,

00:18:17.700 --> 00:18:20.280
and one day, it'll explode in a supernova.

00:18:20.660 --> 00:18:22.450
Wow...

00:18:22.990 --> 00:18:27.210
But after a while, I wasn't
able see that boy anymore.

00:18:27.960 --> 00:18:30.710
I never had the chance to say goodbye to him.

00:18:31.540 --> 00:18:34.920
I never found out his name, either.

00:18:36.510 --> 00:18:40.720
I started to think it must have
been a dream or an illusion.

00:18:41.390 --> 00:18:43.810
I'd forgotten about that until now...

00:18:46.180 --> 00:18:47.640
Minato?

00:18:48.270 --> 00:18:50.480
I'd thought it was an illusion, as well.

00:18:50.940 --> 00:18:55.150
But it wasn't, was it, Subaru?

00:18:58.740 --> 00:18:59.610
This is...

00:19:00.030 --> 00:19:01.820
Betelgeuse.

00:19:03.660 --> 00:19:04.740
It's bright...

00:19:08.210 --> 00:19:09.920
It's neutrino light.

00:19:10.580 --> 00:19:12.130
Right now, at this very moment,

00:19:12.130 --> 00:19:16.590
Betelgeuse's central core is collapsing
at the speed of light.

00:19:16.590 --> 00:19:18.380
A supernova explosion.

00:19:18.920 --> 00:19:23.390
It will still take several more days before
the star itself begins collapsing.

00:19:24.220 --> 00:19:29.390
And it will take another six hundred and
fifty years before this reaches Earth.

00:19:29.940 --> 00:19:33.270
There's nothing that can convey it faster
than the speed of light, after all.

00:19:34.610 --> 00:19:36.730
That's why we have to forget it?

00:19:37.110 --> 00:19:40.030
Yes, everything that happens here.

00:19:41.530 --> 00:19:43.410
What if we don't go back?

00:19:43.410 --> 00:19:44.240
Huh?

00:19:45.030 --> 00:19:47.450
If we never went back, would we
be able to remember it?

00:19:47.830 --> 00:19:50.000
Would that stop it from being undone?

00:19:51.460 --> 00:19:52.330
Subaru...

00:19:53.710 --> 00:19:56.420
I'm the magic user from back then.

00:20:15.480 --> 00:20:17.440
The sun is setting.

00:20:24.110 --> 00:20:26.320
Subaru, what's wrong?

00:20:27.240 --> 00:20:28.540
I don't know.

00:20:28.950 --> 00:20:32.790
I don't know why, but I'm crying.

00:20:36.460 --> 00:20:39.550
Well, it's almost done, so we should finish up.

00:20:39.550 --> 00:20:40.380
Yeah.

00:20:43.130 --> 00:20:47.140
Can we still turn in the interview with
the couple on the day of the event?

00:20:48.390 --> 00:20:50.890
I'll never be able to sleep tonight.

00:20:51.600 --> 00:20:55.690
Oh, it looks like I forgot to
bring the observatory key.

00:20:56.650 --> 00:20:57.610
Minato?

00:20:58.110 --> 00:21:00.820
Should I lock it and then return
the key to the staff room?

00:21:00.820 --> 00:21:03.110
Oh, no, I'll do it.

00:21:03.450 --> 00:21:06.660
You should head home before it gets dark.

00:21:07.070 --> 00:21:08.370
Yeah, but...

00:21:08.830 --> 00:21:11.410
I feel like doing it today.

00:21:13.460 --> 00:21:15.790
S-Sure... Thank you.

00:21:28.220 --> 00:21:28.260
Observatory

00:21:57.040 --> 00:21:58.170
Subaru...

00:21:58.630 --> 00:22:01.130
It looks like this is where we say goodbye.

00:22:02.170 --> 00:22:05.050
To Be Continued

00:22:12.220 --> 00:22:16.690
You see, when I looked up

00:22:16.690 --> 00:22:22.070
everyone was smiling at me

00:22:22.070 --> 00:22:31.780
both embarrassed and happy as the starry sky turned sideways

00:22:31.780 --> 00:22:40.750
Ever since then, whenever my daily life seemed hopeless

00:22:35.330 --> 00:22:38.120
...my daily life...

00:22:40.750 --> 00:22:50.510
I'd go into myself just for a little bit and ask

00:22:50.510 --> 00:22:52.390
"Can I fly?"

00:22:52.390 --> 00:22:56.600
"Sky" shall be our meeting point

00:22:56.600 --> 00:23:02.230
We can go there whenever we want to

00:23:02.230 --> 00:23:11.910
The wind sows stars in the far distance only light leaps to

00:23:11.910 --> 00:23:16.540
"We have to catch them!"

00:23:16.540 --> 00:23:21.040
In the very moment I reached out my hand,

00:23:21.040 --> 00:23:26.380
the scenery around us glittered

00:23:26.630 --> 00:23:31.090
sometime after school

00:23:36.390 --> 00:23:38.350
Just where did those two go?

00:23:38.350 --> 00:23:40.600
They probably went home already.

00:23:40.600 --> 00:23:42.440
But their bags are still here.

00:23:42.440 --> 00:23:44.610
Okay, let's go find them!

00:23:44.610 --> 00:23:46.570
Next episode: Shining Night.

00:23:46.570 --> 00:23:49.440
You're way into this, Itsuki!
